senses.gloss:
mádhu, a. sweet; as n. sweet food and
drink: esp. Soma; milk and its products;
oftenest honey, 26^13. [cf. μέθω, ‘wine’;
AS medu, Eng. mead.]

madhyamá,
 —1. midmost, situated between;
 —2. of middling quality, size, etc.;
 —3. as m. n. the middle (of the body),
waist;
 —4. as n. the middle (of anything).
[mádhya, 474: cf. 525^3.]
